029,2.0974 51.3454,2.0171 51.2896,1.9322 51.2359,1.8447 51.185,1.7564 51.1373,1.6695 51.0933,1.5859 51.0537,1.5077 51.0189,1.4368 50.9895,1.3753 50.9763,1.3473 50.9638,1.3198 50.952,1.293 50.9409,1.2666 50.9306,1.2408 50.9213,1.2155 50.913,1.1907 50.9057,1.1663 50.8995,1.1424 50.8946,1.1189 50.8909,1.0958 50.8886,1.0731 50.8877,1.0507 50.8884,1.0287"]}],"category":["Met"],"certainty":"Possible","description":"Information on update: Warning area extended into more of eastern and southeastern England. A broad band of thunderstorms and heavy rain will move north across England and Wales on Thursday, perhaps becoming slow moving in the afternoon and evening. Accumulations of 20-30 mm in an hour is possible locally, while 30 to 40 mm can be expected fairly widely and up to 50 mm in a 12 hour period in places. There is a small chance that some places may see more than 50 mm in three hours and more than 75 mm through 12 hours, especially over east facing high ground. Lightning and hail of 1-2 cm will also be hazards. \n\nFor further details see https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","event":"Yellow thunderstorm warning","expires":"2026-08-27T21:00:00+00:00","headline":"Thunderstorms and heavy rain may lead to some disruption.: UPDATED","instruction":"Consider if your location is at risk of flash flooding. If so, consider preparing a flood plan and an emergency flood kit.\n\nGive yourself the best chance of avoiding delays by checking road conditions if driving, or bus and train timetables, amending your travel plans if necessary.\n\nPeople cope better with power cuts when they have prepared for them in advance. It's easy to do; consider gathering torches and batteries, a mobile phone power pack and other essential items.\n\nIf you find yourself outside and hear thunder, protect yourself by finding a safe enclosed shelter (such as a car). Do not shelter under or near trees, or other structures which may be struck by lightning. If you are on an elevated area, move to lower ground.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change quickly: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.","language":"en-GB","onset":"2026-08-27T04:00:00+00:00","parameter":[{"value":"2; Yellow; Moderate","valueName":"awareness_level"},{"value":"3; Thunderstorm","valueName":"awareness_type"},{"value":"Where flooding or lightning strikes occur, there is a chance of delays and some cancellations to train and bus services","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Spray and sudden flooding could lead to difficult driving conditions and some road closures","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Some communities might become cut off if roads flood","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Flooding of homes and businesses could happen quickly, with damage to some buildings from floodwater, lightning strikes","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Power cuts might occur and other services to some homes and businesses could be lost","valueName":"impacts"}],"responseType":["Prepare"],"senderName":"UK Met Office","severity":"Moderate","urgency":"Immediate","web":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings"}],"msgType":"Update","references":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings,2.49.0.0.826.0.GB_260825092316_fe1f3f25.v1.0.T,2026-08-25T09:23:16+00:00 https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings,2.49.0.0.826.0.GB_260826085739_fe1f3f25.v2.0.T,2026-08-26T08:57:39+00:00 https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings,2.49.0.0.826.0.GB_260826162556_fe1f3f25.v3.0.T,2026-08-26T16:25:56+00:00","scope":"Public","sender":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","sent":"2026-08-27T06:48:15+00:00","source":"2.49.0.0.826.0.GB","status":"Actual"},"raw_properties":{"supersededByAlertId":null,"supersededAt":null,"supersedeType":null,"geometryDescription":"geometry is bbox only, link (member of the feature's links array) with type application/geo+json points to geojson describing the exact shape","geometryType":"bbox","OBJECTID":"a96ae433-7c0b-4da3-af9a-4c92f0f817a6","alertId":"379a5472-1969-46c2-8020-0b297510ea5d","countryCode":"UK","featureType":"polygon","hubLanguage":"en-GB","indexArea":0,"indexFeature":0,"indexInfo":0,"hubTime":"2026-08-27T06:48:46Z","hubLink":"https://meteo.fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com/api/archive/warnings/379a5472-1969-46c2-8020-0b297510ea5d.xml?AWSAccessKeyId=DO00LYPLJBWUUWC6D6NU&Expires=1787860578&Signature=YZlsNZUOVe%2FKug0LPTKNoacCQOI%3D"}},{"alert_id":"meteo_32bd63a2-df37-4500-bf7f-5493dbf76bda","source":"ukmetoffice","title":"Yellow thunderstorm warning","description":"An area of heavy, thundery rain is expected to develop across France this afternoon and then run north across or close to parts of southeast and east England overnight. While there is a chance that the rain will remain offshore in the North Sea, it is more likely than not to affect at least parts of the highlighted area, which could see frequent lightning, hail and strong, gusty winds in addition to heavy rain. Some places may receive 30-50 mm of rain, much of this falling in less than three hours, with a lower chance of 50-75 mm in a few spots. There is a lot of uncertainty in the development and track of this weather system, but impacts currently look most likely in the north of the warning area later in the night, with clearer, drier conditions following from the south. \n\nFor further details see https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","instruction":"Consider if your location is at risk of flash flooding. If so, consider preparing a flood plan and an emergency flood kit.\n\nPrepare to protect your property and people from injury. Before gusty winds arrive, check to ensure moveable objects or temporary structures are well secured. Items include: bins, garden furniture, trampolines, tents, gazebos, sheds, and fences.\n\nGive yourself the best chance of avoiding delays by checking road conditions if driving, or bus and train timetables, amending your travel plans if necessary.\n\nPeople cope better with power cuts when they have prepared for them in advance. It's easy to do; consider gathering torches and batteries, a mobile phone power pack and other essential items.\n\nIf you find yourself outside and hear thunder, protect yourself by finding a safe enclosed shelter (such as a car). Do not shelter under or near trees, or other structures which may be struck by lightning. If you are on an elevated area, move to lower ground.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change quickly: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.","headline":"Thunderstorms may bring impacts from flooding, lightning or hail overnight.","area_desc":"East Midlands | East of England | London & South East England | Yorkshire & Humber","severity":"moderate","certainty":"possible","urgency":"future","tag":["thunderstorm"],"start_date":"2026-08-27T16:00:00+00:00","end_date":"2026-08-28T06:00:00+00:00","geometry":{"coordinates":[[[1.0781,50.8143],[1.0393,50.8223],[1.0005,50.8395],[0.962,50.8648],[0.9239,50.897],[0.8863,50.935],[0.8495,50.9776],[0.8135,51.0239],[0.7786,51.0726],[0.7449,51.1227],[0.7125,51.173],[0.6817,51.2225],[0.6525,51.2701],[0.6252,51.3146],[0.5999,51.355],[0.5798,51.3883],[0.5621,51.4212],[0.5465,51.4537],[0.5325,51.486],[0.5199,51.5181],[0.5083,51.5502],[0.4974,51.5823],[0.4867,51.6147],[0.4759,51.6473],[0.4647,51.6803],[0.4528,51.7139],[0.4397,51.748],[0.4251,51.7828],[0.4086,51.8185],[0.3861,51.8647],[0.3621,51.9131],[0.3368,51.9632],[0.3104,52.0146],[0.283,52.067],[0.2548,52.1198],[0.226,52.1728],[0.1968,52.2254],[0.1673,52.2773],[0.1376,52.3281],[0.108,52.3774],[0.0786,52.4248],[0.0496,52.4698],[0.0212,52.5122],[0.0002,52.5419],[-0.0208,52.5704],[-0.0419,52.5977],[-0.0629,52.6241],[-0.084,52.6497],[-0.1052,52.6747],[-0.